speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I believe there is also unanimous consent for the following motion. I move:
That the Special Committee on the Review of the CSIS Act and the Security Offences Act be authorized to travel to Washington, D.C. for the period from TUesday, March 20, 1990 to Thursday, March 22, 1990 for the purpose of holding discussions respecting security intelligence administration and structure, and that the necessary staff do accompany the committee;
and that the committee be authorized to travel to Vancouver for the period from March 25, 1990 to March 28, 1990 for the purpose of hearing evidence related to the committee's order of reference and of visiting regional police and security facilities, and that the necessary staff do accompany the committee.
